            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of lipoma of the corpus callosum by CT in five cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The value of CT in the easy diagnosis of lipomas and associated anomalies of the corpus callosum, thus avoiding angiography and pneumoencephalography, is reported in five cases. An angiogram was performed in only one of the five cases and provided no additional diagnostic information.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
